  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0-alpha - First release whose nodes actually appear in vvvv.\n\n      The 0.0.x line (0.0.1 - 0.0.4, now unlisted) installed and contributed no nodes at\n      all, for three independent reasons, none of which produced an error message:\n      malformed document IDs in VL.GIS.vl (VL requires exactly 22 characters, first in\n      [A-V]); a missing UTF-8 BOM; and no [assembly: ImportAsIs] on the forwarded\n      assemblies, without which their public statics are demoted to raw .NET reflection\n      nodes that the NodeBrowser hides.\n\n      The entry point is now generated rather than hand-written, and all three failure\n      modes are asserted before release.\n\n      Also in this release: node categories are GIS.Geometry / GIS.Projection /\n      GIS.Serialization / GIS.Tiles / GIS.Mesh.*; VL.GIS.Stride is renamed VL.GIS.Mesh\n      since it never referenced Stride; minimum vvvv version is now gamma 7.2.\n\n      The GIS functionality itself remains essentially untested - see the README.",
